WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.746
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B two, Book one.

2
00:00:05.046 --> 00:00:09.025
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.325 --> 00:00:15.716
Unit ten: Online Safety. Today you will give safety rules with 'should be' + past participle.

4
00:00:16.016 --> 00:00:18.703
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.667 --> 00:00:23.050
Part one: words. You will learn twelve new words.

6
00:00:23.917 --> 00:00:25.336
Cybersecurity.

7
00:00:26.350 --> 00:00:30.300
Cybersecurity means protecting computers and data from attacks.

8
00:00:30.917 --> 00:00:33.276
Cybersecurity is a growing career.

9
00:00:33.883 --> 00:00:37.325
Your turn. Say: Cybersecurity.

10
00:00:40.167 --> 00:00:41.795
Cybersecurity.

11
00:00:42.550 --> 00:00:43.307
Phishing.

12
00:00:44.317 --> 00:00:47.767
Phishing means fake messages that try to steal your information.

13
00:00:48.383 --> 00:00:50.383
That email was a phishing trick.

14
00:00:50.983 --> 00:00:53.403
Your turn. Say: Phishing.

15
00:00:56.267 --> 00:00:57.012
Phishing.

16
00:00:57.750 --> 00:00:59.088
Two-factor authentication.

17
00:01:00.083 --> 00:01:04.091
Two-factor authentication means a second code that proves it is really you.

18
00:01:04.683 --> 00:01:06.927
Turn on two-factor authentication.

19
00:01:07.517 --> 00:01:10.831
Your turn. Say: Two-factor authentication.

20
00:01:13.667 --> 00:01:15.330
Two-factor authentication.

21
00:01:16.083 --> 00:01:17.340
Data privacy.

22
00:01:18.350 --> 00:01:21.603
Data privacy means keeping personal information safe.

23
00:01:22.217 --> 00:01:24.518
Read the app's data privacy rules.

24
00:01:25.117 --> 00:01:27.978
Your turn. Say: Data privacy.

25
00:01:30.833 --> 00:01:32.334
Data privacy.

26
00:01:33.083 --> 00:01:34.177
Cyberbullying.

27
00:01:35.183 --> 00:01:37.717
Cyberbullying means bullying someone online.

28
00:01:38.317 --> 00:01:41.094
Cyberbullying can hurt as much as bullying at school.

29
00:01:41.683 --> 00:01:44.614
Your turn. Say: Cyberbullying.

30
00:01:47.467 --> 00:01:48.712
Cyberbullying.

31
00:01:49.450 --> 00:01:50.811
Digital footprint.

32
00:01:51.817 --> 00:01:54.408
Digital footprint means everything you leave online.

33
00:01:55.017 --> 00:01:57.446
Your digital footprint can last forever.

34
00:01:58.050 --> 00:02:00.795
Your turn. Say: Digital footprint.

35
00:02:03.633 --> 00:02:05.029
Digital footprint.

36
00:02:05.783 --> 00:02:07.144
Secure password.

37
00:02:08.150 --> 00:02:11.996
Secure password means a strong password that is hard to guess.

38
00:02:12.583 --> 00:02:15.755
A secure password mixes letters, numbers and symbols.

39
00:02:16.350 --> 00:02:19.002
Your turn. Say: Secure password.

40
00:02:21.867 --> 00:02:23.309
Secure password.

41
00:02:24.050 --> 00:02:25.341
Online predator.

42
00:02:26.350 --> 00:02:30.590
Online predator means an adult who tries to harm young people online.

43
00:02:31.183 --> 00:02:34.425
Never share your address; an online predator could use it.

44
00:02:35.017 --> 00:02:37.704
Your turn. Say: Online predator.

45
00:02:40.567 --> 00:02:42.009
Online predator.

46
00:02:42.750 --> 00:02:43.995
Report abuse.

47
00:02:44.983 --> 00:02:49.049
Report abuse means to tell the platform or an adult about harmful behaviour.

48
00:02:49.650 --> 00:02:51.615
Click the button to report abuse.

49
00:02:52.217 --> 00:02:55.287
Your turn. Say: Report abuse.

50
00:02:58.133 --> 00:02:59.460
Report abuse.

51
00:03:00.217 --> 00:03:01.253
Encrypted.

52
00:03:02.250 --> 00:03:04.981
Encrypted means changed into a secret code.

53
00:03:05.583 --> 00:03:07.444
Encrypted messages are safer.

54
00:03:08.050 --> 00:03:10.540
Your turn. Say: Encrypted.

55
00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:14.471
Encrypted.

56
00:03:15.217 --> 00:03:16.136
Scam.

57
00:03:17.150 --> 00:03:19.161
Scam means a trick to steal money.

58
00:03:19.750 --> 00:03:22.693
'You won a free phone!' is usually a scam.

59
00:03:23.283 --> 00:03:25.460
Your turn. Say: Scam.

60
00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:29.208
Scam.

61
00:03:29.950 --> 00:03:31.230
Safe browsing.

62
00:03:32.217 --> 00:03:35.308
Safe browsing means visiting only trusted websites.

63
00:03:35.917 --> 00:03:38.450
Safe browsing protects your device.

64
00:03:39.050 --> 00:03:41.946
Your turn. Say: Safe browsing.

65
00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:46.091
Safe browsing.

66
00:03:46.900 --> 00:03:50.876
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:03:51.717 --> 00:03:55.226
Visal, what steps do you take to stay safe online?

68
00:03:56.317 --> 00:04:00.290
I use a secure password and two-factor authentication.

69
00:04:01.383 --> 00:04:03.313
What about strange emails?

70
00:04:04.417 --> 00:04:08.509
Phishing emails should be deleted. Their links should not be clicked.

71
00:04:09.617 --> 00:04:11.233
And if you see cyberbullying?

72
00:04:12.317 --> 00:04:17.172
Abuse should be reported immediately, and a trusted adult should be told.

73
00:04:18.333 --> 00:04:19.822
Part three: grammar.

74
00:04:20.683 --> 00:04:23.333
Grammar focus: Passive with should.

75
00:04:23.633 --> 00:04:24.820
Look at the pattern.

76
00:04:25.517 --> 00:04:28.085
Passwords should be kept secure.

77
00:04:28.983 --> 00:04:31.111
Abuse should be reported immediately.

78
00:04:32.017 --> 00:04:33.947
Strange links should not be clicked.

79
00:04:34.900 --> 00:04:40.046
Use 'should be' + past participle for rules when the person doing the action is not important.

80
00:04:40.783 --> 00:04:44.469
Be careful! Don't say: Passwords should kept secure.

81
00:04:46.433 --> 00:04:48.828
Say: Passwords should be kept secure.

82
00:04:49.128 --> 00:04:51.069
The passive needs 'be' after 'should'.

83
00:04:51.867 --> 00:04:54.275
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:04:55.067 --> 00:04:56.602
Staying Safe Online.

85
00:04:56.902 --> 00:05:01.456
Using two-factor authentication and a secure password protects your data privacy.

86
00:05:02.467 --> 00:05:05.952
Phishing emails should be deleted without clicking any links.

87
00:05:06.967 --> 00:05:09.512
Your digital footprint should be checked regularly.

88
00:05:10.500 --> 00:05:14.171
Reporting cyberbullying keeps online spaces safer for everyone.

89
00:05:15.167 --> 00:05:18.525
Abuse should be reported immediately to a trusted adult.

90
00:05:19.633 --> 00:05:23.275
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:05:24.117 --> 00:05:26.174
Passwords should be blank secure.

92
00:05:26.474 --> 00:05:29.628
A, kept. B, keep. C, keeping.

93
00:05:33.167 --> 00:05:34.737
The answer is A: kept.

94
00:05:35.883 --> 00:05:38.754
Fake messages that try to steal information are blank.

95
00:05:39.054 --> 00:05:42.649
A, phishing. B, encrypted. C, browsing.

96
00:05:46.200 --> 00:05:47.944
The answer is A: phishing.

97
00:05:49.083 --> 00:05:52.012
Everything you leave online is your digital blank.

98
00:05:52.312 --> 00:05:56.012
A, footprint. B, password. C, privacy.

99
00:05:59.567 --> 00:06:01.694
The answer is A: footprint.

100
00:06:02.900 --> 00:06:06.017
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:06:06.883 --> 00:06:09.556
What steps do you take to stay safe online?

102
00:06:18.350 --> 00:06:19.990
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:06:20.290 --> 00:06:28.108
I use a strong password and never share it. Strange links should not be clicked, and bullying should be reported to an adult.

104
00:06:28.408 --> 00:06:30.106
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:06:31.017 --> 00:06:35.027
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and passive with should.

106
00:06:35.327 --> 00:06:40.000
Today's value is online safety. Keep your password secret and be kind online.

107
00:06:40.300 --> 00:06:42.848
See you in Unit eleven. Goodbye!

108
00:06:43.148 --> 00:06:46.671
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

